workedExamples.solution_text:
For $0\le x<3$:
$\begin{align*}F(x)&=\int_0^x\frac16\,dt\\&=\frac x6.\end{align*}$
The probability accumulated up to $3$ is $F(3)=\frac12$.
For $3\le x\le5$:
$\begin{align*}F(x)&=\frac12+\int_3^x\frac14\,dt\\&=\frac12+\frac{x-3}4\\&=\frac{x-1}4.\end{align*}$
Thus
$F(x)=\begin{cases}0,&x<0,\\\dfrac x6,&0\le x<3,\\\dfrac{x-1}4,&3\le x\le5,\\1,&x>5.\end{cases}$
Both pieces give $F(3)=\frac12$, and $F(5)=1$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=3cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[black,->] (-0.7,0)--(6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-0.12)--(0,1.2) node[above] {$F(x)$};
\draw[black,thick] (-0.6,0)--(0,0)--(3,0.5)--(5,1)--(5.8,1);
\draw[black,dashed] (0,0.5)--(3,0.5)--(3,0);
\draw[black,dashed] (0,1)--(5,1)--(5,0);
\path (0,0.5) node[left] {$\frac12$} (0,1) node[left] {$1$} (3,0) node[below] {$3$} (5,0) node[below] {$5$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*}P(2<X<4)&=F(4)-F(2)\\&=\frac34-\frac13\\&=\frac5{12}.\end{align*}$

For $-3\le x\le0$:
$\begin{align*}F(x)&=\int_{-3}^x\frac{3+t}{9}\,dt\\&=\left[\frac{(3+t)^2}{18}\right]_{-3}^x\\&=\frac{(3+x)^2}{18}.\end{align*}$
The accumulated probability is $F(0)=\frac12$.
For $0<x\le3$:
$\begin{align*}F(x)&=\frac12+\int_0^x\frac{3-t}{9}\,dt\\&=\frac12+\left[-\frac{(3-t)^2}{18}\right]_0^x\\&=1-\frac{(3-x)^2}{18}.\end{align*}$
Thus
$F(x)=\begin{cases}0,&x<-3,\\\dfrac{(3+x)^2}{18},&-3\le x\le0,\\1-\dfrac{(3-x)^2}{18},&0<x\le3,\\1,&x>3.\end{cases}$
The pieces agree at $0$, and $F(-3)=0$, $F(3)=1$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.8cm,y=3cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
